#### 6. Factual Sources & Consumer Protection Gates
- **Bureau of Indian Standards (BIS):** Mandatory 3-symbol hallmarking (BIS triangular logo, purity fineness mark 750/585, and 6-digit alphanumeric laser HUID on the earring post).
- **Ministry of Consumer Affairs & Legal Metrology:** Net weight billing requirements. Retail jewellers must deduct the exact gemstone weight in carats (1 ct = 0.200 g) from the gross weight and bill gold strictly on net weight.
- **Gemological Institute of America (GIA) & IGI:** Ruby evaluation standards, corundum mineralogy ($Al_2O_3$), chromium trace color chemistry, rutile silk inclusions, and traditional heat treatment stability vs composite lead glass filling hazards.
- **Goods and Services Tax (GST):** Uniform 3% GST on precious jewellery in India.

